cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "three-procedural-locomotion: procedural human locomotion for Three.js"
message: "If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  TypeScript library for Three.js that makes a humanoid character walk, run,
  turn, crouch, jump and go to a point over any ground without baked
  animations. Everything is computed every frame from a speed and a heading:
  gait, footstep planning, Two-Bone IK legs, foot placement on the terrain and
  the posture of the body.
authors:
  - family-names: Mesquida
    given-names: Pablo
    website: "https://pablopx.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PabloMesquida/three-procedural-locomotion"
url: "https://locomotion.pablopx.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Three.js
  - procedural animation
  - procedural locomotion
  - character animation
  - inverse kinematics
  - footstep planning
  - TypeScript
